{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 12, :comments ["<b>Wise in his own eyes</b> — to his own seeing, and he is the sluggard. And the proof: 'wise, sluggard in his own eyes.'" "<b>Hope</b> — its meaning: better to be a fool than him, than the sluggard. Another interpretation: the fool has hope that what he hopes for from El will come to him, more than the sluggard."], :book :proverbs, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 26, :notes {1 "Reading יקוה in the first interpretation as 'better to be'; the phrase is compressed and the syntax is ambiguous."}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Proverbs -- Daat" "http://www.daat.ac.il/he-il/tanach/parshanut_hamikra/full-text/eben-ezra/mishley/"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T19:24:50.672158068Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}